{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>You will be sated</b> with shame rather than the honor you sated yourself with, for your day of calamity comes — and this is “you too will drink.” And <b>הערל</b> is from the nif'al paradigm, like <b>והאסף</b> (and you will be gathered). The meaning: you will see your foreskin as though written <b>ותערל</b>, like <b>ומות</b> (and die) on the mountain." "<b>The cup of YHWH's right hand will turn upon you, and disgrace</b> — one word and the peh is doubled, as it begins each word, like <b>בבת</b> (pupil of) his eye. Or perhaps they are two words and the alef is missing, like <b>ככלב</b> (like a dog) returning to its vomit."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:02.325301074Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}